(7739208, 1275855, 141319, '<td valign="top">I LIKE this. Maybe your aperture should have been a tiny bit smaller to get the center wheels and the reflection into focus as well- JMO</td>', 'I LIKE this. Maybe your aperture should have been a tiny bit smaller to get the center wheels and the reflection into focus as well- JMO', '2023-02-27 03:57:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7739242, 1276100, 27608, '<td valign="top">Sorry to see your DQ :(  I always get nervous with image validation, even when I haven''t done much in the way of editing.  I do import into LR, so I may need to watch out when doing JPG.  <br/> <br/>I''m pretty lazy, but at the same time my flow is pretty quick.  I download the RAW file to my iPhone and then upload to LR to do basic editing on my phone almost in real time.  From there at some point I will sign into my PC, export the original to my photo folder + export the edit as a JPG.  Lastly I export to PS for any intensive edits / resize and sharpening.  I very rarely take out my CF or SD cards to plug them manually into my PC.  Final final steps are I backup my images to an external drive before clearing them off my camera''s cards.</td>', 'Sorry to see your DQ :(  I always get nervous with image validation, even when I haven''t done much in the way of editing.  I do import into LR, so I may need to watch out when doing JPG.   I''m pretty lazy, but at the same time my flow is pretty quick.  I download the RAW file to my iPhone and then upload to LR to do basic editing on my phone almost in real time.  From there at some point I will sign into my PC, export the original to my photo folder + export the edit as a JPG.  Lastly I export to PS for any intensive edits / resize and sharpening.  I very rarely take out my CF or SD cards to plug them manually into my PC.  Final final steps are I backup my images to an external drive before clearing them off my camera''s cards.', '2023-02-27 12:40:31.000000', NULL, 0),
